{
  "company_name": "DistroCapital Finance",
  "industry": "Industrial Distribution",
  "use_case": "Working capital and cash flow optimization for industrial distribution",
  "space_title": "DistroCapital Finance - Working Capital & Cash Flow \ud83d\udcb0",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Industrial Distribution\n\n**Use case:** Working Capital & Cash Flow Optimization\n\nDistroCapital Finance \u2014 treasury and working-capital analytics across 20 business units spanning pipe & valve, industrial supply, electrical, welding, safety, and corporate. The CFO and Treasurer use this space for cash position, DSO/DPO, and cash conversion cycle; Branch Managers and Segment GMs use it to track AR collections, AP timing, and inventory investment by region.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Cash conversion cycle (CCC) days \u2014 industrial distribution typical 60-90 days, best-in-class <45\n- DSO (Days Sales Outstanding) \u2014 target 30-45 days for B2B industrial\n- DPO (Days Payable Outstanding) \u2014 target 30-45 days; widen carefully to preserve vendor terms\n- Net cash flow ($) \u2014 inflow minus outflow over period\n- Current ratio \u2014 healthy 1.5-2.5x; <1.0 is a liquidity warning\n- AR balance and inventory investment ($) \u2014 capital tied up in operations\n- Liquidity status mix (Strong/Adequate/Tight/Critical) \u2014 risk concentration\n- Forecast variance (actual vs forecasted cash flow) \u2014 treasury planning accuracy\n\n**Data sources**\n- `business_units` \u2014 daily cash transactions (customer/vendor payments, payroll, transfers) with inflow/outflow and AR collected\n- `cash_transactions` \u2014 weekly working-capital snapshots: AR balance, AP balance, inventory investment, DSO, DPO\n- `working_capital_snapshots` \u2014 monthly forecast vs. actual cash flow with CCC, current ratio, and liquidity status",
